condition_name: Xerophthalmia
condition_slug: xerophthalmia
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: "Xerophthalmia is a spectrum of eye diseases that leads to loss of corneal integrity and is often associated with Vitamin A deficiency. The disease ranges from night blindness to conjunctival xerosis, to Bitot's spots, to corneal xerosis and finally keratomalacia."
clinical_features[1]:
  - type: Clinical Features
    features[5]: Night blindness,Dryness of the conjunctiva and cornea (xerosis),Tearing,Bitot's spots,Corneal degeneration (keratomalacia)
investigations[2]: Conjunctival impression cytology (where available),Serum Vitamin A levels
treatment:
  goals[0]:
  non_drug[1]: Nutrition education
  drug[3]: "Vitamin A capsules 200,000 units orally daily for two days, then one capsule after one week",Topical antibiotics (ointment) and antivirals where applicable,Padding the eye (for active corneal ulceration)
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[1]: Avoid the use of harmful traditional eye medication
  supportive_measures[0]:
differential_diagnoses[1]: Measles keratoconjunctivitis
complications[3]: Corneal perforation,Corneal scarring,Blindness
prevention[3]: Distribution of massive dose capsules of vitamin A to affected communities,Nutrition and health education,Fortification of foods with vitamin A
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment: null
prognosis: null